      "message": "imo, a \"decorator\" pattern is actually a better design pattern for this. \n\nIn the new proposal, PythonBinaryModule \"inherits\" from PythonLibraryModule. But a python binary is not a special kind of python library - one is not interchangeable with the other.\n\nbuild/soong/cc uses a similar decorator pattern. FWIW, build/soong/java does not (even though I think it should too).\n\nCan you give some more context on what is driving this refactor? Does it make maintenance/bp2build etc. easier?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 10,
        "startChar": 24,
        "endLine": 12,
        "endChar": 29
      },
      "revId": "75a1b99a73efada271f269cd4c2a5b5172044d8c",
